# One conversation between a phone and the agent, frame by frame (see the plan document, "Phone and agent
# protocol" and its "Message reference" tab). tests/agent/test_agent.cpp writes this file and fails when the
# agent no longer says exactly this; the Android app's tests read it to learn what the agent sends.
#
# The link is a Bluetooth serial one, so each side gives 4,096 bytes as its largest frame, and the phone
# has to be paired and to do `auth` before the agent tells it anything. It is paired here: before the
# pairing.issue that is answered `rejected`, a controller on the head unit's local socket, which is not
# in this file, opened the pairing window, and the code it was given is the one in the pairing.issue
# after that. The key in that answer is the K of the two proofs of `auth`; tests/test_protocol_vectors.py
# works both out again from this file. At the end the same controller ends the phone's pairing: the
# agent's last frame is the event link.closing, with which it says that it closes the link and why, and
# a phone app that reads it closes its side of the link at once.
#
#   magic HEX   the bytes the phone, which dialled, sends before its first frame
#   > HEX       a frame from the phone to the agent
#   < HEX       a frame from the agent to the phone
#
# A line that starts with # shows the next frame's payload if it is a message. The phone's lines are examples
# of what the agent accepts; another client may order the members of its messages differently. The agent's
# lines are what this agent sends when it is in the same state: a head unit with nothing installed, the
# test key as its only package key, 500,000,000 bytes free everywhere, the head-unit id, plan ids, pairing
# code, pairing key and nonce that the test's counter gives, and a clock that stands still, so
# job.progress comes only when something changes and no ping is due. The package is
# tests/packages/runtime-2.1.0 as tests/make_packages.py builds it.

magic 4e42544c

# {"id":1,"method":"info.get","params":{}}
> 01000000280000007b226964223a312c226d6574686f64223a22696e666f2e676574222c22706172616d73223a7b7d7de8bb9ec8
# {"id":1,"error":{"code":"bad-state","message":"hello comes first"}}
< 01000000430000007b226964223a312c226572726f72223a7b22636f6465223a226261642d7374617465222c226d657373616765223a2268656c6c6f20636f6d6573206669727374227d7d271809df
